                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Kind of like a western Final Fantasy game with slow pacing, the humor was the best aspect of the game but I found the gameplay and the battle system not to be interesting enough to carry the whole game. Fun to play for a couple of hours at a time, but it failed to get me hooked. I like how the game explains all its features in the terms of its world. Exemplified by savepoints being critters called timeminders that live in all the alternate realities simultaneously, with their tears acting as the item that resurrects dead party members. The game has a great lore, artstyle and humor, but unfortunately they don't make it a good game. Maybe they were just influenced by the wrong kind of games, only Eddie knows.",
